{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:51:01.854264Z","id":"c502e8b87faced1764769b965d37f2b1fb0916256d34270310731e2c48eedb92","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:acb06db94cb825ed096dfe96b9336cb4c05b6de8","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:64:69 as b1696811 in git:acb06db9","supersedes":"421abeee4eaaa480188e5b9dc62819f47bd4a79c8c125a09228caebc9c131cff","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:41:08.964875Z","id":"a50126d1c3cc8e14fa9ecc7459223653b81507ae36bdb5a9b0a9de2e6370965e","body":{"detail":"create places a hook question with no body thread_id in the suggestion's where.thread_id when where.artifact_id is the question's artifact (test api_questions::a_hook_question_after_a_thread_delivery_is_placed_in_that_thread). The hook never sends thread_id, so without this a hook question is never shown inside a thread, even when Clax instigated the work at one (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md §2, 'the thread it arose from'). The suggestion's thread is the session's last delivered thread (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs place_of), used only while the delivery is newer than the last terminal prompt; a question about other work in the same turn would still land in that thread.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":325},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"2ce0937541a053b3b8e4e5b079de3cf14714742c1598f4970c592b04fbca54b7"},"summary":"A mirrored (hook) question takes only a thread_id its body names, and is never placed in the suggestion's thread","tags":["revisit:hook questions show up in threads they were not about","design","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:41:08.964966Z","id":"33f4136588cf1216dfabf8b433e7dfcd57267cc5bd74f53d72537be384b32333","body":{"detail":"Store::take_late_answers (crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs:1011) returns pulled in-terminal questions (Ask me here, POST /api/questions/<qid>/pull) beside answered and declined ones, and late_answers here renders every row that is not Declined with the answered head and no answer lines. Since d41601bde the pull route exists and wakes the session's feedback polls, so a pulled question is handed to the agent as an answer with no answers instead of 'the person wants this question in Clax'. The view in the poll's answers carries pulled: true.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"f9c0c2d7d0d5edbebdecd134f2d0abc310fd6255e1af32cfae54b676aca72ad6"},"suggested_fix":"Render rows with pulled_at set as their own block telling the agent to ask the question again with ask, and keep them out of the answered head.","summary":"A pulled in-terminal question reaches the agent as 'The person answered your question' with no answers","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:22:17.238585Z","id":"7eb804ae2eb91c753eaf1d60c8531f7da9dc34bf1c7ea3df9e196b6495af6200","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:39105e3ef","summary":"late_answers renders a pulled row with pulled_block (\"The person wants your question ... asked in Clax instead\"), never the answered head; a hook question's block says its terminal dialog stays until Esc. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all --test_arg=api_where_to_ask:: passes a_late_answer_and_a_pull_are_deliveries_from_clax_at_their_thread (asserts no 'answered your question') and a_pulled_hook_question_says_its_terminal_dialog_stays_until_esc.","supersedes":"33f4136588cf1216dfabf8b433e7dfcd57267cc5bd74f53d72537be384b32333","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:16:44.618800Z","id":"0041ec0ac8b12516c268e0fe839d7c0a953c1f1a561802fc11fe861e8837cdcc","body":{"detail":"A pull (POST /api/questions/{qid}/pull) reaches the agent as pulled_block in late_answers, on the next feedback tier that polls (a tool result, the prompt hook, a Stop hook), like a late answer. The Claude Code channel (<channel source=\"plugin:clax:clax\" ...>) carries only comment notices (artifact_id, thread_id, comment_id), so a pull cannot wake an idle Claude Code session the way a comment sent to it can. Not done because a channel notice names a comment to read with comments_read, and a pull has no comment.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"cf5a681dabfef8a4135164580168ec43199cddf8a50a85e3b2bf26c1e151cab0"},"summary":"Deliver Ask me here through the Claude Code channel notice rather than the late-answer tiers","tags":["revisit:Claude Code channel notices carry more than comments (a question or a pull)","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:16:44.619685Z","id":"9cd440af16a7ee63614e38f7aca1f5102344359dcc57e22dcd260e5eca70d2c1","body":{"detail":"The names shipped differ from the spec's. The MCP tool, Pi tool, route and fields are where_to_ask (MCP tool where_to_ask in crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs, Pi clax_where_to_ask, GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask handled here, the ask result's where_to_ask field, {where_to_ask, signals}), because 'attention' already names each viewer's attention per artifact (crates/clax-store/src/attention.rs, GET /api/viewers/me/attention, the artifact JSON's attention). The spec's 'notice' questions are in_terminal (the questions.in_terminal column of migration 37 in crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs, ask {in_terminal: true}, web/shell/src/q/TerminalCard.svelte, error not_in_terminal), because 'notices' already names GET /api/sessions/{id}/notices (feedback::notices, Grok's monitor). Path not taken: the spec's names attention and notice, which would give both words a second meaning. Question for the owner: keep where_to_ask and in_terminal, or rename (and amend the spec to match either way).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"665cea1fd43bf746688c4fab513521810c3d7da57c7a335efbccf817494721dc"},"summary":"Name the suggestion 'attention' and the terminal-asked question a 'notice', as spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md and its plan do","tags":["naming","status:needs-decision","revisit:the owner chooses other names for the suggestion or the in-terminal question","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.526422Z","id":"6d9a56f5b255ad11342acc9fdd90faa2cee43f8b805e4b66e072af9c2d424555","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1360:1376, record be332351. CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1223},"end":{"line":1264},"content_hash":"81457863f5a6f37f002514515cebebced86ea812b3069431a7be337d750945e9"},"summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"12e45a31044836310cd745b632533ae5cb3b502bb75033e2e79073c0b1649093","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/guards.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.549061Z","id":"0a65af984b96d87186f00c5ab46c4c9534b92fe9f3b89398fc08c5d435994a04","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:1757:1783, record 67937f34. Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:acb06db9","span":{"start":{"line":1813},"end":{"line":1840},"content_hash":"6cce876e324df5229bc43d9cb8fef99778d482642c51a693a6f98c18e4f83838"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"2278fadd7d83cab8cc47d67cf920517b0b7ff55c09942c4e431b12d4d590e464","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.571632Z","id":"e99ee821c0e07ecbcfcc5c340fb2ac110e6672be40aa9fb17bc112aa915333de","body":{"detail":"Live seats refuse every artifact write a person makes as themselves (threads, db, room). POST /api/questions/<qid>/answer and decline, and PUT /api/viewers/me/seen and looked, are not seat-checked: a question is the person's exchange with their own agent and not an artifact write, and seen and looked are the viewer's private marks. Decide whether 'read only' covers them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":749},"end":{"line":749},"content_hash":"0ae91d3100d18ff23c480c4637c371f61a5eef5ffa3c280690c00ad759664cc0"},"summary":"Answering one's own agent's question, and the seen and looked marks, are not refused to a spectator","supersedes":"12db18b83147f579fce6a873699cf31d595d074d95f56f3cc3f8b671855570c2","tags":["live-seats","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.978785Z","id":"998c19b0f6fee2ae3520b49a2931992aa419a72003f0d2094866ea1e81fd2f85","body":{"detail":"The daemon tells an agent from the owner by the agent-channel marker and session headers, which an agent on the owner's machine can leave out; it can already delete artifacts or answer questions the same way (answers given with the daemon token count as answered_via cli, which the push approval refuses, crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs approval). Requiring the owner's browser (or the extension) for every push, as for answering, would close it at the cost of `clax push` by hand. Which does the owner want?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":564},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"c2e11c8e7ca8b6fbf439e7068988cde5ea974d204708cf3b87cd1a287e887499"},"summary":"Only publish_public asks the owner: an agent that runs the CLI as the owner (CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, or curl with the daemon token) pushes without asking","supersedes":"0728cf04053f5ad016502341b34a338ea13e3c11decdbe20b6c3d72acc65e2a7","tags":["security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:08.001703Z","id":"3adceb3bf97de0422b726ab4fea38e1aacf09281c0b5c34ab8a0f87ca8b1d2e8","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":159},"content_hash":"1bb871416cb1ea49f8c3e022eb2900e0d61ee9a9be5e5ad1e692a0b0fa63bde3"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","supersedes":"32769653a05b120daf3c1eb81c07c32c20b2b94fa0bc3d74a3665b255883eff8","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.217923Z","id":"969c27617616d2bd5bc4eccdaf926abcda2b609f367dfb743dc201be0e97c388","body":{"detail":"create places a hook question with no body thread_id in the suggestion's where.thread_id when where.artifact_id is the question's artifact (test api_questions::a_hook_question_after_a_thread_delivery_is_placed_in_that_thread). The hook never sends thread_id, so without this a hook question is never shown inside a thread, even when Clax instigated the work at one (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md §2, 'the thread it arose from'). The suggestion's thread is the session's last delivered thread (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs place_of), used only while the delivery is newer than the last terminal prompt; a question about other work in the same turn would still land in that thread.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":326},"end":{"line":334},"content_hash":"2ce0937541a053b3b8e4e5b079de3cf14714742c1598f4970c592b04fbca54b7"},"summary":"A mirrored (hook) question takes only a thread_id its body names, and is never placed in the suggestion's thread","supersedes":"a50126d1c3cc8e14fa9ecc7459223653b81507ae36bdb5a9b0a9de2e6370965e","tags":["revisit:hook questions show up in threads they were not about","design","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.240573Z","id":"a084d9827c5f5406ec88bcfb1804381217cfe68d03054afa0577d06b1d6037cd","body":{"detail":"Live seats refuse every artifact write a person makes as themselves (threads, db, room). POST /api/questions/<qid>/answer and decline, and PUT /api/viewers/me/seen and looked, are not seat-checked: a question is the person's exchange with their own agent and not an artifact write, and seen and looked are the viewer's private marks. Decide whether 'read only' covers them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":750},"end":{"line":750},"content_hash":"0ae91d3100d18ff23c480c4637c371f61a5eef5ffa3c280690c00ad759664cc0"},"summary":"Answering one's own agent's question, and the seen and looked marks, are not refused to a spectator","supersedes":"e99ee821c0e07ecbcfcc5c340fb2ac110e6672be40aa9fb17bc112aa915333de","tags":["live-seats","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.452316Z","id":"30f8f5757607c763bac45858669ab98112b8155d9d4a750f6f0463aac90fc877","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":588},"end":{"line":623},"content_hash":"39fe6a4fe8b96bf9fee95422225eb4b4e569264cd0c206f1371a24dfc10e2ec6"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"6213635be19c356b2d9831790871738f8714a104f67dde0613e768f006669e14","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.483911Z","id":"33e5df8cb597bad28aff82b316e374b44ca33c219df46b81fbae2c45d60f999d","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":609},"end":{"line":609},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"300ee61fe75092fdf8889355a930839fb6e30217ae18cbcdc2bf9f848e7084b8","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:14:24.971510Z","id":"46924ac503cc9406d839a05763e27c25a3d508e01f782fabaab83fc5b296f2fe","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9cd440af16a7ee63614e38f7aca1f5102344359dcc57e22dcd260e5eca70d2c1","summary":"questions.in_terminal (and the rest of this branch's schema) is now migration 38 in crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs; 37 is the repair of databases migrated with earlier copies of 24 to 26, 30 and 36 (REPAIR_MIGRATION).","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:00:49.797297Z","id":"6fe270b23ca32bab7578924aa0eae47a26ef19bedb3bc857d33a792353532ced","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. The send now asks that agent's person for every author of the thread they have not approved (Store::send_to_named routes, spec §9.2), so nothing is delivered without that person's approval; but nothing in the comment's answer names the agent's person, so the commenter is not told whose agent it reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":521},"end":{"line":556},"content_hash":"245896ea2a31dbd8a6375a0fa7572bf2f093d35ee3d40edc60a8713df27dba78"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"16293258bc7748739fbf62dc7f4ec95e5af08e121fc44eeb095625de96c399bf","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:00:49.929255Z","id":"8727b91693af95ad757fea2ff176bf067f00d5ed6ad79d2852fb5e0b209e918a","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":542},"end":{"line":542},"content_hash":"20fb897884082f66581aaae4c04a83c9d1e2c433b40aea73a1a440a9a722ac9f"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","supersedes":"ede1c137c61df7ef3808273ab3f05bd98d3172fad7fc0641c510157e0aaab4dd","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356074Z","id":"ba839dc22b0b62d3285527c255ab1c700b718ada070854f9fb095ac63f274d66","body":{"detail":"fork takes Agent<ArtifactsFork>, which admits Caller::Person (fork_refusal handles it). For a browser caller Identity::caller (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:299-391) never reads or checks header_session; only grant and token callers have it validated. fork then calls session_header(&headers) (artifacts.rs:1094) and publishing_session(st, &session, grant=None) (artifacts.rs:1102), which accepts any live session whose grant_id is None, i.e. any of the owner's agent sessions. fork_artifact_async (crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs:83-200) stores it as the fork's owner_session_id and as version 1's session_id, and ensure_watch (artifacts.rs:1112) makes that owner agent watch the person's fork, so the person's later comments there are routed to the owner's agent as if it published the page. create and publish are not exposed this way because they take TokenOrAgent. Session IDs are stripped from browser views (strip_sessions), which narrows who can name one, but the handler should not depend on that.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1094},"end":{"line":1113},"content_hash":"f6f7f1245f9076b6c4ff8c6a4ea2e55d5d68556f1c2970d60c223e0084298815"},"suggested_fix":"Take the session from the verified caller instead of the raw header: `let session = a.caller.session().map(str::to_string);` (None for Person/Owner-browser callers), or refuse X-Clax-Session with 400 when !a.caller.is_agent(). Add an api test where a Person cookie forks with X-Clax-Session naming an owner agent session and assert the fork has no owner_session_id and no watch.","summary":"fork reads X-Clax-Session raw for every caller, so a connected person's browser can attribute its fork to an owner's agent session and make that session watch it","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356161Z","id":"3d1ff28002d90caa359de3b3e3b0ea58776c61e7b5544295658329e1eacc3349","body":{"detail":"lookup reads file_meta and, for a file that is not text/html, returns its bytes at once (content.rs:193-194); only the wrapped-page path checks st.get_artifact (content.rs:196). delete_artifact_async (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:368-458) only sets artifacts.deleted_at and leaves the versions rows, so file_meta still answers; it then removes the content repository and on failure only logs 'could not remove deleted artifact's files' (artifacts.rs:450-456). In that case, and in the window between the delete's commit and the repository removal (the read takes no content lock), GET /a/<aid>/<n>/<file> keeps serving a deleted artifact's images, scripts and data to anyone holding the URL, with Cache-Control immutable (content.rs:309-318), while its index answers 404.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":194},"content_hash":"509498c32d87e6071cc25fcb676f5b01c64daab354fa07787d8b149ec5c7ab15"},"suggested_fix":"Check the artifact row before the raw branch: move `st.get_artifact(&id)?.ok_or(CoreError::NotFound)?;` above `if !always_wrap && !is_html(...)` in lookup (one indexed read), and add a test that deletes an artifact whose content removal fails (a content store stub) and asserts a supporting file answers 404.","summary":"A version's non-HTML files are served without checking that the artifact still exists","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356230Z","id":"4a99cab1ea600c2be9e97416061e6b8b1031475d4516ddc9a326e0aa84a3a49c","body":{"detail":"has_viewer is `who.owner_browser() || who.cookie.is_some()` (artifacts.rs:478), but the attention it guards is added whenever who.browser_viewer(st) names a viewer (artifacts.rs:514-516), and browser_viewer uses names_viewer(), which also counts hosted_viewer (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:260-263, 446-452). On a hosted daemon a signed-in person's or guest's request carries hosted_viewer with cookie None (identity.rs:162-169), so their per-viewer `attention` is answered without `Cache-Control: private, no-cache` and `Vary: Cookie` (artifacts.rs:526-534), unlike the owner's. A shared cache in front of the hosted daemon may then serve one viewer's attention to another.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":478},"end":{"line":534},"content_hash":"6e3490abebee564ff5ed042769e440dab84ba72ff0a67cb7c7d2761d4849d87e"},"suggested_fix":"Use `let has_viewer = who.owner_browser() || who.names_viewer();` so the header follows the same rule that decides whether attention is included, and cover a hosted viewer's GET in the hosted api tests.","summary":"GET /api/artifacts/<aid> marks a viewer's answer private only for a clax_viewer cookie, not for a hosted session's viewer","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356285Z","id":"29aaf55978127ca5ca1d27b21b6bbeb87b8cbf6ab4f577d528a931fa4c6e5e96","body":{"detail":"AckBody's thread_ids and comment_ids (feedback.rs:735-740) have no length cap; ack passes them whole to Store::acknowledge and acknowledge_comments (feedback.rs:770-784), whose acknowledge_where (crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs:1546-) runs a query per ID. Only the default JSON body limit bounds them, so one request with tens of thousands of IDs holds a store worker for the whole loop. Other ID-list routes cap theirs: inbox read takes at most MAX_MARK_IDS = 500 (inbox.rs:31, 514), threads:send MAX_BATCH_THREADS, viewers MAX_LOOKUP_IDS = 64 (viewers.rs:139), working MAX_WORKING_THREADS.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":733},"end":{"line":791},"content_hash":"4e93d7f54ce7c3cdd3e400650f6b4f212e16a08feefa818dd60dd343cb540497"},"suggested_fix":"Add a MAX_ACK_IDS (for example 500, as inbox's MAX_MARK_IDS) and answer 400 invalid_json when either list exceeds it, before store_call; document the cap in the handler's doc comment and docs/contract.md.","summary":"POST /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback/ack takes unbounded thread_ids and comment_ids lists and acknowledges them in one store call","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:40.356317Z","id":"c3cd21b02cb719005e6156b117397abed028fb77d468af8a38b37cbc1bee639a","body":{"detail":"token() checks only that the peer is a loopback address and Host is a literal local name (token.rs:33-41), then answers {\"token\": s.token}. docs/contract.md (Security model, around line 6082) says state-changing routes need the token 'from <CLAX_HOME>/daemon.json (mode 0600)', implying only the owner's OS user holds it, and says an owner agent 'runs as the owner's OS user' when it notes it can fetch the token. On a machine with several OS users (or a sandboxed process with loopback network but no file access), any of them can GET http://127.0.0.1:<port>/api/token and act as the owner, bypassing the file mode. The contract does not state that loopback is trusted as the owner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"6afd754aefd043f6b9953b98d0d1876af97793f8b2ee5472c65d65b29c4e905d"},"suggested_fix":"Either state in docs/contract.md's Security model that every local user and process is trusted at the owner's level, or restrict /api/token to browser requests (require Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin and an Origin of the daemon's own host, which a non-browser process can forge but which at least keeps it to the shell's flow) and, on platforms that allow it, check the peer's UID (SO_PEERCRED / LOCAL_PEERCRED on a Unix socket, or bind a per-user Unix socket for the token). Record the choice as a waiver if loopback trust is intended.","summary":"GET /api/token hands the daemon token to any process on the machine, including other OS users, which the 0600 daemon.json does not","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717144Z","id":"04784729156856a1533fd4b2c57a02a4f2fd381942241850fa071a1696cf08d4","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:362-370: a clax_viewer cookie yields Caller::Person without reading header_session (only the grant branch, 311-337, and the token branch, 341-348, check it). crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:1094 session_header(&headers) reads the raw header; 1095 a.grant() is None for Person (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:722-727); publishing_session (artifacts.rs:132-153) then accepts any live session whose grant_id is None, i.e. any owner agent session. fork_artifact_async receives it as session_id (artifacts.rs:1103-1110) and ensure_watch runs on it (1111-1113). fork_refusal (artifacts.rs:1018-1031) admits Caller::Person with create rights; person_agent_session (agent.rs:910-918) only rejects PersonAgent without a session. Concern severity fits: it needs a known owner session ID, which strip_sessions hides from browsers.","kind":"comment","references":"ba839dc22b0b62d3285527c255ab1c700b718ada070854f9fb095ac63f274d66","summary":"confirmed: fork takes X-Clax-Session raw for a Person caller and publishing_session accepts any live owner-agent session (grant None)","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717371Z","id":"73715aeefd32119f14eadbfceb3197e08b3d724b5d69fa0817658a26f3fab385","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:192-194 returns Served::Raw after st.file_meta only; st.get_artifact is first called at 196, on the HTML path. Store::file_meta (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1524-1529) uses get_version (1488-1504), whose SELECT_VERSION (814-819) reads `versions` alone with no join to artifacts.deleted_at. delete_artifact_async (artifacts.rs:368ff) sets deleted_at and deletes many dependent tables but not versions, then on content-removal failure only logs \"could not remove deleted artifact's files\". The file route (content.rs:265-282) does no other existence check before lookup; the raw response carries http_cache::IMMUTABLE (content.rs:313-318).","kind":"comment","references":"3d1ff28002d90caa359de3b3e3b0ea58776c61e7b5544295658329e1eacc3349","summary":"confirmed: lookup returns a non-HTML file's bytes before any artifact-row check, and file_meta reads versions with no deleted_at filter","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717538Z","id":"d161c308f8b4334b075cea0051bce9d74dd29f5ec75b0d614a94e880ce49a347","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:478 `let has_viewer = who.owner_browser() || who.cookie.is_some();` vs 514-516 `if let Some(viewer) = who.browser_viewer(st)? { v[\"attention\"] = ... }`. browser_viewer (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:446-452) is true for owner_browser() || names_viewer(), and names_viewer (259-262) is cookie.is_some() || hosted_viewer.is_some(); owner_browser (425-428) covers hosted_owner but not hosted_viewer. The doc on hosted_viewer (identity.rs:166-170) says cookie is None there. So a hosted person's or guest's response with attention takes the else branch (artifacts.rs:535-536) with no Cache-Control/Vary. No global layer adds them: the only hosted Cache-Control inserts are no_store on sign-in responses (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1683-1687, crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:996-997).","kind":"comment","references":"4a99cab1ea600c2be9e97416061e6b8b1031475d4516ddc9a326e0aa84a3a49c","summary":"confirmed: has_viewer ignores hosted_viewer while browser_viewer, which gates attention, counts it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717705Z","id":"040819efb1c8148092b33430caf05d9327fcf0dba5f1eb3d18dcb2188ca7e262","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs:733-740 AckBody has Option<Vec<String>> with no cap; ack (749-791) checks only that one is present, then calls st.acknowledge and st.acknowledge_comments with the whole slices. crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs:1573-1582 runs one prepared query per ID inside a single with_tx. Other ID-list routes cap: crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs:31 MAX_MARK_IDS = 500 (checked 514), viewers.rs:139 MAX_LOOKUP_IDS = 64 (checked 171), working.rs:47 MAX_WORKING_THREADS. The caller must hold the token or a grant (TokenOrAgent), so concern, not blocker, fits.","kind":"comment","references":"29aaf55978127ca5ca1d27b21b6bbeb87b8cbf6ab4f577d528a931fa4c6e5e96","summary":"confirmed: ack passes uncapped thread_ids/comment_ids into a per-ID query loop inside one transaction","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:23.717866Z","id":"d0a82866b931982b5614cdad6aa815532f5cccb9a8f4f8b0e019f01a9c729dc4","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs:33-47: the only checks are is_loopback(addr) and is_local_host(host); the body is {\"token\": s.token} for any such request, same-origin or not (the Sec-Fetch-Site check at 48-50 only adds cookies). docs/contract.md:6082-6083 ties state-changing routes to the token \"from <CLAX_HOME>/daemon.json (mode 0600)\"; 6107-6110 justifies an owner agent fetching /api/token because it \"runs as the owner's OS user\"; 6167-6173 describes the loopback rule but nowhere states that other OS users or processes on the machine are trusted at the owner's level. Concern severity fits: a documentation gap or accepted risk, not a defect a single-user install hits.","kind":"comment","references":"c3cd21b02cb719005e6156b117397abed028fb77d468af8a38b37cbc1bee639a","summary":"confirmed: GET /api/token gates only on a loopback peer and a local Host, so any local OS user or loopback-only sandbox gets the token","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:35:16.117221Z","id":"32f297a721a275a3f55c42abeca512e2f1c2ab3a3fcd68e553a612788b19a291","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts is TokenOrAgent and takes any files: opening it to people's browsers would let a browser publish arbitrary HTML as a person, and the brief thread would be a second request the browser makes. POST /api/artifacts:new writes the placeholder itself (clax_core::brief::placeholder_html, the title escaped) and the brief thread in one store call, deleting the artifact when the thread cannot be written.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":635},"content_hash":"f49358eafb33e98a156891cbbed79487f972b03369b36a6b93961a0ee14081c0"},"summary":"Let the browser publish the placeholder through POST /api/artifacts instead of a route of its own","tags":["revisit:the gallery lets people paste or upload a page of their own","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:35:16.117676Z","id":"d8ef18074e9eecdbcf14a25893036c458f753b79ca688be52ef1b993ca740c51","body":{"detail":"Watches are TokenOrAgent: a session subscribes itself. A browser adding a watch for any session would bypass the approval routing that a send naming an agent does (Store::send_routed, Route::Send). Instead a person's send {to} may name any live agent that may read and watch the artifact, giving it a watch exactly as an @name in their comment does (resolve_named): no new authority, and the approval path is the existing one. Agents keep the old rule (they hand threads off), and so do guests and LAN viewers and batch sends.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1196},"end":{"line":1235},"content_hash":"002de5d38485f823c7849ddb74c214758a74cbb70287d94b06f71ed865779fc6"},"summary":"Attach the picked agent with PUT /api/sessions/<sid>/watches/<aid> from the browser, or a route of its own","tags":["revisit:guests or LAN viewers need to attach agents from a Send menu","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:35:16.118568Z","id":"d2a62dc61cd966d4ec578b1e49fb1de46007e87fc69c7f5f37cee72aca6ad8f2","body":{"detail":"The brief is written with announce_new_thread(mention=false, named=None): an @ in it sends nothing. The dialog's picker is the one way the brief reaches an agent, so a refused @name (agent_cannot_read) can never fail the artifact's creation after it was made.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":635},"content_hash":"f49358eafb33e98a156891cbbed79487f972b03369b36a6b93961a0ee14081c0"},"summary":"Act on @agent and @name in the brief as in any viewer comment","tags":["revisit:people write @name in briefs expecting it to send","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:35:16.119187Z","id":"299d57e8452e92e12580ac75c3693b8882e9a60eefed6adca8020d82ab216ce1","body":{"detail":"Live seats are per artifact (docs/contract.md 'Live seats and spectators'); there is no gallery-wide spectator state. A new artifact is its maker's, so their seat there is reserved (clax_http::seats::claim_for: created_by), and they write and send its brief. brief_refusal checks the person's rights (create, read own, comments write) and refuses guests, but no seat. tests api_hosted::people_start_artifacts_from_briefs_and_guests_may_not shows Kim, a spectator on Plan, creating. If 'spectators may not create' means something else (for example refusing a person who is a spectator anywhere right now, or capping creation while seats are full), that needs a rule the seat model does not have yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":468},"end":{"line":510},"content_hash":"9bc6384c666632a0dd535666fef9943ec306bae9b30f09ed3511067d51fb0c4a"},"summary":"Spectators: a person beyond another artifact's live seats may start an artifact from a brief","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:03:42.259819Z","id":"878ca21d8974db3b16af3f38daa9c96e9a13cafafa6a631635f8a941242512b8","body":{"detail":"Callers of GET /api/token: the shell (web/shell/src/api.ts:103, a same-origin browser fetch; its bearer token signs the shell's writes and the response sets the owner and events cookies), the demo driver (demo/lib/http.ts:114, a Node process with no Sec-Fetch-Site), the extension worker (web/extension/src/sw/worker.ts:70-72, stubbed to 204), and the hosted daemon's own branch (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1384, 1527, the shell token in place of the daemon token). The skills tell agents never to fetch it (plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md, checked by scripts/test-plugins.sh:485), and docs/contract.md:6110-6116 already accepts that an owner agent running as the owner's OS user can. Other routes trust loopback too: live pages are visible to any loopback peer (docs/contract.md, Security model), so the question is wider than this handler.\n\nOptions:\n(A) Document loopback trust: state in docs/contract.md's Security model that every process and OS user able to reach the loopback port is trusted at the owner's level (the 0600 daemon.json guards the token at rest, not the daemon), and record a waiver on token.rs:28-47. No behaviour change; multi-user machines stay exposed.\n(B) Require Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin and an Origin of the daemon's own host on /api/token. Stops only a naive fetch (any process can set both headers); demo/lib/http.ts:114 would need to send them. Little real protection.\n(C) Check the peer's OS user. TCP gives no peer UID on macOS without platform calls (the workspace forbids unsafe, so libproc FFI is out; lsof per request is slow); a Unix socket gives it (LOCAL_PEERCRED / SO_PEERCRED) but a browser cannot use one, so the shell would need another route to the token.\n(D) Stop handing the token out by loopback alone: the CLI (`clax open`, crates/clax-commands/src/commands/open.rs, which runs as the owner and can read daemon.json) opens the shell with a one-use code that /api/token exchanges for the token and the owner cookie; a browser that opens the gallery without one is a viewer until the next `clax open`. Closes the hole for other OS users and sandboxes without file access; changes how the owner's browser becomes the owner (bookmarks, a restarted daemon) and needs the demo driver and the e2e fixtures (web/e2e/fixtures.ts:216-221, web/e2e/streams.spec.ts) reworked.\n\nRecommendation: (A) now, as a waiver plus the contract sentence, since Clax targets single-user machines and live pages already trust loopback; (D) if multi-user machines or loopback-only sandboxes become a supported setting.","kind":"comment","references":"c3cd21b02cb719005e6156b117397abed028fb77d468af8a38b37cbc1bee639a","summary":"Needs the owner's call: whether any local process or OS user with loopback access is trusted at the owner's level, which decides how /api/token is closed","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:08:02.219342Z","id":"8d7c85f3dea9517b743f9133534d246dcf2a8764f06d8fb951a5535edbeccb20","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:50951558b","summary":"Fixed: has_viewer uses who.names_viewer(), so a hosted session's viewer gets Cache-Control private and Vary Cookie; api_hosted::an_artifacts_answer_with_a_signed_in_viewers_attention_is_private passes (failed before).","supersedes":"4a99cab1ea600c2be9e97416061e6b8b1031475d4516ddc9a326e0aa84a3a49c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:08:02.262715Z","id":"5bbc8890e55344422ab821f5e9653f6ac97f26550bb0209b687116daa2a8327b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f4699d186","summary":"Fixed: fork takes its session from the verified caller (a.caller.session()); api_forks::a_persons_browser_cannot_fork_as_an_owner_agent_session passes (failed before), an_agent_session_forks_and_watches_its_fork still passes.","supersedes":"ba839dc22b0b62d3285527c255ab1c700b718ada070854f9fb095ac63f274d66","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:08:02.439600Z","id":"5fdb6814fd5c16d8ad5f6f655c73c3dcb8e6dd783ea53d59efaf2746b9a9d867","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:584fdd8e4","summary":"Fixed: content lookup reads the live artifact before file_meta; api_content::a_deleted_artifacts_files_are_not_served_while_its_content_remains passes (failed before).","supersedes":"3d1ff28002d90caa359de3b3e3b0ea58776c61e7b5544295658329e1eacc3349","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:08:02.578379Z","id":"a690283369da7d69cdbf45e1078a41a519bfe7e021360a54c06b9f4495d73773","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e9c9d6637","summary":"Fixed: MAX_ACK_IDS = 500 enforced with 400 invalid_json; MCP client, Pi client and linked sync chunk; api_feedback::ack_takes_at_most_its_cap_of_ids_per_list and comments::acknowledgements_past_the_daemons_cap_go_in_chunks pass.","supersedes":"29aaf55978127ca5ca1d27b21b6bbeb87b8cbf6ab4f577d528a931fa4c6e5e96","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:36:46.677771Z","id":"c107137ca74c4383b02771bd859e185fd8e640d2d5a7dc90a7c71dcbba528b2c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3093025901aad08add351fe2dea5b9445b7cbe6393781175bcd7a886d6277372","summary":"Same defect as record b8ab7260 (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs); fixed by git:05be14efd: the key is looked up and recorded inside the thread's or comment's own transaction (Store::create_thread_keyed_async, add_comment_keyed, add_agent_reply_keyed), and record_comment_key is removed. Test: clax-store linked::tests::a_keyed_thread_or_comment_is_made_once_with_its_key; the clax-server integration groups 1-6 pass.","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:02:15.191985Z","id":"4696f1a5eda10d9634890089275e0feab9037693b039f7eda82ad8c57ef7f321","body":{"detail":"git:551c720f0 looks the key up and records it inside the thread's or comment's own transaction (Store::create_thread_keyed_async, add_comment_keyed, add_agent_reply_keyed) and removes record_comment_key; test: clax-store linked::tests::a_keyed_thread_or_comment_is_made_once_with_its_key. git:5a978209f makes a resend go through the route and do the sends its first write may not have reached (create_thread_keyed_now on Keyed::Before; the comment route's replayed comment); test: clax-server tests/api_linked.rs a_resent_keyed_write_does_the_sends_its_first_write_did_not_reach, which fails on 551c720f0 (assertion failed: sent(&t.id)).","kind":"comment","references":"3093025901aad08add351fe2dea5b9445b7cbe6393781175bcd7a886d6277372","summary":"Same defect as record b8ab7260 (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs); fixed by git:551c720f0 and git:5a978209f","supersedes":"c107137ca74c4383b02771bd859e185fd8e640d2d5a7dc90a7c71dcbba528b2c","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:23:05.637232Z","id":"5f1f58a145c8ebcd05601301e34d70b75bda9b6a2c5add315797f0f6f735bcdb","body":{"detail":"A replayed viewer comment runs its sends again when Store::comment_has_feedback (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:1416) finds no feedback row, which cannot tell a send that was lost from a comment that never needed one: such a comment re-runs resolve_named and a Route::Join send_routed with the thread's state at the resend (a Join may count the comment into open approval requests a second time). A replayed thread (create_thread_keyed_now, line 651) announces with the resend's body for its @mentions, not the stored first comment's. Both are idempotent for feedback rows; neither is covered beyond tests/api_linked.rs a_resent_keyed_write_does_the_sends_its_first_write_did_not_reach.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1125},"end":{"line":1140},"content_hash":"862f9f79e70123c5d03b35decdca61e33160d9b9b1ae21c105782032f83c0bbd"},"summary":"A keyed write's replay re-runs its follow-up with the state at the resend, not the first write's","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.236444Z","id":"49e1428a299836d17ece9542a3c79ab9d3a5860ab02784258213292a6d21a665","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fde797b85","summary":"Fixed (fde797b85, 70b6e33ce): a keyed thread or comment records its comment_keys row in the transaction that writes it, and a resend does the sends its first write did not reach; api_linked::a_resent_keyed_write_does_the_sends_its_first_write_did_not_reach passes (failed before).","supersedes":"3093025901aad08add351fe2dea5b9445b7cbe6393781175bcd7a886d6277372","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
